From: d4r
Subject: [PATCH] dxil-spirv: AGS B-to-C binary16 transfer without LDS on gfx12

An AGS conversion from an FP8 B matrix to a binary16 accumulator (the RR
stages' FP8 decodes) converts in B, then changes the use through an LDS
round trip with two subgroup barriers, as only FP8 took the element-wise
copy. With wmma_fp8 (gfx12), B and C keep a lane's column with rows
i + 8 * half-wave for 16-bit elements too, so binary16 takes the copy as
well. The round trip's 4 KiB of LDS halved the RR decoders' occupancy; the
outputs are bit-identical.

---
diff --git a/subprojects/dxil-spirv/opcodes/dxil/dxil_ags.cpp b/subprojects/dxil-spirv/opcodes/dxil/dxil_ags.cpp
--- a/subprojects/dxil-spirv/opcodes/dxil/dxil_ags.cpp	2026-10-26 14:36:39.896352288 +0100
+++ b/subprojects/dxil-spirv/opcodes/dxil/dxil_ags.cpp	2026-10-26 14:36:39.901325940 +0100
@@ -534,11 +534,15 @@
 	{
 		if (get_matrix_type(input_imm) != AmdExtD3DShaderIntrinsicsWaveMatrixType_A &&
 		    get_matrix_type(output_imm) != AmdExtD3DShaderIntrinsicsWaveMatrixType_A &&
-		    get_type_data_format(input_imm) == AmdExtD3DShaderIntrinsicsWaveMatrixDataFormat_FP8)
+		    (get_type_data_format(input_imm) == AmdExtD3DShaderIntrinsicsWaveMatrixDataFormat_FP8 ||
+		     get_type_data_format(input_imm) == AmdExtD3DShaderIntrinsicsWaveMatrixDataFormat_F16))
 		{
 			// It appears that in the cases we care about, layout of B and C are the same.
 			// Just do element-wise copy here to avoid the bad roundtrip.
 			// This assumption only seems to hold for FP8, but that's the only case we care about.
+			// d4r: also binary16 on gfx12 (wmma_fp8), where B and C keep a lane's column with
+			// rows i + 8 * half-wave for 16-bit elements too: the FP8 -> F16 B-to-C conversion
+			// (an FP8 decode) converts in B, then took this LDS round trip and its barriers.
 			return emit_coopmat_transfer(impl, v, input_imm, output_imm);
 		}
 	}
